      R'=0.4850  |Q|=3  m_R=0.0921 m_Q=0.6905  R=(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13)
      R'=0.5004  |Q|=4  m_R=0.1441 m_Q=0.6190  R=(1, 2, 3, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13)
      R'=0.5397  |Q|=3  m_R=0.1274 m_Q=0.6905  R=(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12)

 (2) DOES NOT FACTOR:
   (2a) coverings with R'!=1 (SPEC!=0, relation couples R&Q): 953/956 (relation does NOT factor)
   (2b) extremal {1..13}: meas(lonely)=0.0 (tight/measure-0 locus); units (Z/14)* = [1, 3, 5, 9, 11, 13] (phi(14)=6);
        antipodal pairs (the BU counting measure, saddle index phi/2=3): [(1, 13), (3, 11), (5, 9)]
        unit fractions a/14 lonely for {1..13} (touch-points): [1, 3, 5, 9, 11, 13] of [1, 3, 5, 9, 11, 13]

 VERDICT: the floor deficit |SPEC|/product stays < 1 set-independently (R' bounded below > 0) even where CV blows up; and the danger relation does not factor (SPEC!=0; at the extremal the lonely set is the multiplicative units in antipodal BU pairs). The 'right frame' is the actual correlation |R'-1|, not the lossy CV -- the Gamma_0(14)/cyclotomic collapse bounds THAT.
